        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prune chat history",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "var rawHistory = $context.$system.$chatHistory;\nvar finalResult = null;\n\nif (rawHistory && rawHistory.trim() !== \"\") {\n    var profileData = \"\";\n    var idSplit = rawHistory.split(\"pPersonId=\");\n    \n    // Extract unique profile IDs and Names\n    for (var i = 1; i < idSplit.length; i++) {\n        var afterId = idSplit[i];\n        var quoteIndex = afterId.indexOf('\"');\n        \n        if (quoteIndex > -1) {\n            var pId = afterId.substring(0, quoteIndex);\n            var tagEnd = afterId.indexOf(\">\");\n            var aEnd = afterId.indexOf(\"</a>\");\n            \n            if (tagEnd > -1 && aEnd > -1) {\n                var pName = afterId.substring(tagEnd + 1, aEnd).trim();\n                var entry = \"Person Name: \" + pName + \"; PersonId: \" + pId + \"\\n\";\n                \n                // Only add if not already in the string (maintains uniqueness)\n                if (profileData.indexOf(entry) === -1) {\n                    profileData += entry;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Extract User turns\n    var userSplit = rawHistory.split(\"USER:\");\n    var userTurns = [];\n    \n    for (var j = 0; j < userSplit.length; j++) {\n        var chunk = userSplit[j].trim();\n        if (chunk !== \"\") {\n            // Isolate everything before AI: responds\n            var aiSplit = chunk.split(\"AI:\");\n            var userText = aiSplit[0].trim();\n            if (userText !== \"\") {\n                userTurns.push(\"USER: \" + userText);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Build the final string with only the last 7 turns\n    var prunedHistory = \"\";\nvar startIdx = userTurns.length > 7 ? userTurns.length - 7 : 0;    \n    for (var k = startIdx; k < userTurns.length; k++) {\n        prunedHistory += userTurns[k] + \"\\n\";\n    }\n\n    // Append context if profiles exist\n    if (profileData !== \"\") {\n        prunedHistory += \"\\n[CONTEXT - Recently Viewed Profiles]\\n\" + profileData;\n    }\n    \n    if (prunedHistory.trim() !== \"\") {\n        finalResult = prunedHistory;\n    }\n}\n\nreturn finalResult;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770901979906"
          },
          "code": "PRUNE_CHAT_HISTORY",
          "id": "1772539706081",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query Planner"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771426250057"
          },
          "code": "QUERY_PLANNER",
          "id": "1770901979906",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770901979908_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a deterministic, production-ready query preparer. Your job: convert one natural-language user request into exactly one JSON object for an execution engine. You must strictly adhere to the schema and logic rules defined below.\n\nSTRICT OUTPUT RULES:\n1. Output exactly one JSON object and nothing else. No markdown, no prose, no commentary.\n2. Omit boolean-controlled fields entirely if their respective flag is false.\n3. Omit any optional filter keys (e.g., orgType, contentType) if they are not explicitly identified. DO NOT return keys with null, empty string, or undefined values, except where explicitly allowed.\n4. Use \"findSemanticMatch\" as the finder. Use ONLY field names defined in SCHEMA STRUCTURE.\n\n### CHAT HISTORY (Past User Intents & Extracted Profiles)\n {{$context.$nodes.PRUNE_CHAT_HISTORY.$output.result}} \n\n---\n\n### 1. UNSUPPORTED INTENT CHECKS (Priority High)\nEvaluate the user query for the following conditions. If ANY are met, set `NotSupportedFlag`: true, populate `NotSupportedReason`, and return the JSON immediately (leave other fields empty/false).\n\n* **Case 1 (Hierarchy/Reporting):** If the user asks for reporting lines, organizational charts, or relationships (e.g., \"who reports to X\", \"X's team\", \"under X\", \"manager of X\").\n    * **STRICT EXCLUSION:** Phrases like \"my team\", \"my reports\", or \"in my team\" must NOT trigger this flag. These are valid talent search filters where security is handled by the execution engine.\n    * *Reason:* \"I do not have access to reporting lines or organizational charts, so I cannot identify managers, direct reports, or team structures.\"\n* **Case 2 (Multi-Person Cold Start):** If the user asks to summarize or compare multiple specific people found in the current input (e.g., \"compare Ravi and John\"), AND their profiles are NOT already present/summarized in `chat_history`.\n    * *Reason:* \"I can compare profiles, but I need to load them first. Please ask me to summarize each person individually, then ask for the comparison.\"\n* **Case 3 (Ambiguity):** If the query relies entirely on subjective adjectives without concrete skills or data points (e.g., \"find ambitious people\", \"fast learners\", \"nice employees\", \"rockstars\").\n    * *Reason:* \"I can only search based on objective data present in employee profiles (e.g., Skills, Certifications, Location, Department). I cannot interpret subjective traits, personality characteristics, or ambiguous criteria.\"\n* **Case 4 (Out of Scope):** If the query pertains to non-talent domains (e.g., Purchase Orders, Contracts, Weather, General Knowledge, Code Generation).\n    * *Reason:* \"I am designed exclusively for Talent Profile Search. I do not have access to data or capabilities outside of this specific domain.\"\n* **Case 5 (Missing Talent Attribute):** If the query ONLY specifies a Location or Organization, but does NOT include any specific talent attributes (e.g., skills, job titles, certifications, or competencies) to search for.\n    * *Reason:* \"Please specify a skill, role, or qualification you are looking for in that location or department.\"\n\n### 2. CONTEXTUAL RELEVANCE & INTENT SHIFTING\nEvaluate if the current user query is a Refinement of the previous search, or a completely New Search (Context Switch). Do NOT rely on specific keywords. Use semantic logic:\n\n* **Refinement (Merge History):** The user uses connecting language (\"and\", \"also\", \"only those\", \"what about\") OR adds a new constraint to the existing topic (e.g., Prev: \"Find Java Developers\" -> Curr: \"in Hyderabad\", or Prev: \"Java devs\" -> Curr: \"those with scrum\"). **Action:** Merge the new constraint with the previous semantic query parameters.\n* **Context Switch (Override):** The user asks for a completely different Role, Skill, or Org (e.g., Prev: \"Find Java Developers\" -> Curr: \"Find Scrum Masters\"). **Action:** The topic has changed; ignore ALL previous filters. Start a fresh query using ONLY the parameters in the current prompt.\n* **Implicit Reset (Override):** If the current query makes complete grammatical sense on its own and does not explicitly reference past filters (e.g., \"Find process engineers in Redwood City\"), treat it as a New Search. Discard previous filters.\n* **Pivot to Person (Ignore Search History):** If the user switches from a generic search to a specific person (e.g., Prev: \"Find Java Developers\" -> Curr: \"Show me Ravi's profile\"). Ignore previous search filters; proceed to Person ID Resolution.\n\n### 3. PERSON ID RESOLUTION\n* If multiple people are mentioned, focus on the primary subject.\n* Inspect `chat_history` for active person mappings in the Context block (formatted as `Person Name: X; PersonId: Y`).\n* Extract the numeric `personId`.\n* If multiple IDs exist, select the one semantically matching the user's reference.\n* If no terminal `personId` is found in history, set `personId`: null.\n\n### 4. PERSON QUERY CONSTRUCTION\n* **Trigger:** If intent is to find a specific person AND `personId` is null.\n* **Action:** Extract the name exactly from the user query. Do NOT normalize/expand.\n* **Construct:** Populate `personQuery` exactly as follows:\n  {\n    \"displayFields\": [\"DisplayName\", \"PersonId\", \"PersonNumber\", \"WorkEmail\"],\n    \"filters\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"DisplayName\",\n        \"term\": \"<name extracted from the user query>\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"securityFilters\": {\n      \"type\": \"PersonSearch\",\n      \"value\": \"AdvancedSearch\"\n    },\n    \"limit\": 500\n  }\n\n### 5. EXTRACTION & PAYLOAD CONSTRUCTION RULES\n* **ORG_STRUCTURE (`orgStructureQueryPayload`):**\n    * Set `resolveOrgStructureFlag`: true if an org is mentioned.\n    * `query`: Core entity name ONLY. Strip \"dept\", \"division\", \"BU\", \"group\", \"branch\". Remove trailing locations (e.g., \"Finance in London\" -> \"Finance\").\n    * `filterCriteria.orgType`: Include ONLY if explicitly labeled (\"DEP\", \"BU\", \"LE\").\n* **LOCATION (`locationFilterPayload`):**\n    * Set `resolveLocationFlag`: true if a physical location is mentioned.\n    * `query`: The geographical entity (e.g., \"Hyderabad\"). Remove \"City of\", \"Region of\".\n    * `filterCriteria`: {\"vectorKey\": \"ORA_LOCATION\"}.\n* **TALENT PROFILE SEARCHES (`talentProfileSearches`):**\n    * **Logic:** Formulate `query` as comma-separated string: Core term + 2-3 professional synonyms/competencies.\n    * **Cleaning:** Remove filler language (\"find people\", \"experts in\", \"who have a\"). Keep \"OR\" logic.\n    * **Content Strategy:** Consider cross-section matches (e.g., Skills are often found in Work History; Certifications in Education).\n    * **Content Types:** Skill, Work History, Certification, Education, Competency, Language, Career/Work Preference.\n    * **Grouping:**\n        * If 1-2 distinct types identified: Create one object per type.\n        * If >2 distinct types: Return ONE object and OMIT `contentType`.\n\n### SCHEMA STRUCTURE:\nReturn a single valid JSON adhering completely with the specified JSON schema. \n\n### CURRENT REQUEST\nuser_query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"NotSupportedFlag\": <boolean>,\n  \"NotSupportedReason\": <string | null>,\n  \"SpecificEmployeeDetailsFlag\": <boolean>,\n  \"personId\": <number | null>,\n  \"personQuery\": <object>,\n  \"resolveOrgStructureFlag\": <boolean>,\n  \"orgStructureQueryPayload\": {\n    \"finder\": \"findSemanticMatch\",\n    \"query\": <string>,\n    \"answerConfiguration\": { \"maximumChunks\": 50, \"minimumSimilarityPercentage\": 70, \"includeSupportingChunks\": true, \"useHybridSearch\": false },\n    \"filterCriteria\": { \"vectorKey\": \"ORA_ORGANIZATION\", \"orgType\": \"DEP\" | \"BU\" | \"LE\" }\n  },\n  \"resolveLocationFlag\": <boolean>,\n  \"locationFilterPayload\": {\n    \"finder\": \"findSemanticMatch\",\n    \"query\": <string>,\n    \"answerConfiguration\": { \"maximumChunks\": 50, \"minimumSimilarityPercentage\": 70, \"includeSupportingChunks\": true, \"useHybridSearch\": false },\n    \"filterCriteria\": { \"vectorKey\": \"ORA_LOCATION\" }\n  },\n  \"talentProfileSearches\": [\n    {\n      \"query\": <string>,\n      \"contentType\": \"Competency\" | \"Education\" | \"Language\" | \"Skill\" | \"Career Preference\" | \"Career Statement\" | \"Work Preference\" | \"Certification\" | \"Work History\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
