        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Locate correct person"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770902696677"
          },
          "code": "LOCATE_CORRECT_PERSON",
          "id": "1770902626679",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770902626681_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a deterministic entity disambiguation agent. Your inputs are a JSON list of people (`person_list_json`), a `user_query`, and `chat_history`.\n\nYour goal is to output a single JSON object indicating if a specific person was identified or if clarification is needed.\n\n### INPUT DATA\n1. Person List - person_list_json: {{$context.$nodes.FIND_PERSON.$output}} \n2. User Query - user_query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n3. History - chat_history: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} \n\n### ALGORITHM\nFollow these steps strictly in order:\n\n1. **Initial Filtering:** - Identify all candidates in `person_list_json` whose `DisplayName` matches the name references in `user_query`.\n\n2. **Contextual Disambiguation (History Check):**\n   - If Step 1 results in **multiple candidates** (ambiguity), check `chat_history`.\n   - specific_check: Was one of these specific candidates (matching by `PersonId`) the subject of the most recent relevant turn in the conversation?\n   - **Yes:** If the history clearly establishes *one* specific `PersonId` that matches the current name query, treat this as a **Match Found** and select that person.\n   - **No:** If history is empty, irrelevant, or refers to a different person not in the current list, proceed to Step 3.\n\n3. **Determine Match Status:**\n   - **Match Found:** If exactly one person remains (either by unique name match in Step 1 OR by history resolution in Step 2), set `matchFoundFlag` to `true`.\n   - **No Match/Ambiguity:** If 0 matches found, or if >1 plausible candidates still exist after history check, set `matchFoundFlag` to `false`.\n\n4. **Construct Clarification (Only if matchFoundFlag is false):**\n   - If `person_list_json` is empty: `userQuestion` = \"No matching employees found with that name.\"\n   - If `person_list_json` has entries, create a conversational question followed by a bulleted list of ALL candidates.\n   - **Start the `userQuestion` with:** \"Which [Name from user_query] can I help you with?\\n\\n\"\n   - **Format:** \"- DisplayName\"\n   - **Duplicate Name Handling:** If multiple entries share the exact same `DisplayName`, you must append a distinguisher to *those specific entries* using this priority check (stop at the first available value):\n     1. `PersonId`\n     2. `PersonNumber`\n     3. `EmailAddress`\n     *Format:* \"- DisplayName (Person ID [DistinguisherValue])\"\n\n### OUTPUT SCHEMA\nReturn ONLY a raw JSON object. Do not use Markdown code blocks.\n\n{\n  \"matchFoundFlag\": boolean,\n  \"personId\": \"number (The PersonId of the match) OR null\",\n  \"userQuestion\": \"String (The clarification text) OR null\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n \"type\": \"object\",\n \"required\": [\"matchFoundFlag\"],\n \"properties\": {\n \"matchFoundFlag\": {\n \"type\": \"boolean\"\n },\n \"personId\": {\n \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"]\n },\n \"userQuestion\": {\n \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n }\n }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
