        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Clean up Person Profile Output",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const raw = $context.$nodes.GET_PERSON_PROFILE_DETAILS.$output;\n\n// Normalize input: Fusion often passes JSON as string\nconst input = (typeof raw === \"string\") ? JSON.parse(raw) : raw;\n\nconst results = input.results || [];\n\nlet personId = null;\nconst sections = [];\n\nfor (let i = 0; i < results.length; i++) {\n const item = results[i];\n const metadata = item.metadata || {};\n\n if (personId === null && metadata.personId != null) {\n personId = metadata.personId;\n }\n\n sections.push({\n sectionContext: metadata.sectionContext || metadata.contentType || null,\n supportingChunks: item.supportingChunks || null\n });\n}\n\n// Assign output to variable named `object`\nconst object = {\n personId: personId,\n sections: sections\n};\n\nreturn object;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770902941177"
          },
          "code": "CLEAN_UP_PERSON_PROFILE_OUTPUT",
          "id": "1770902899420",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prepare Person Data for Reranking",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let searchCombinationResult = $context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_SEARCH_COMBINATION.$output;\nlet personDetails = $context.$nodes.GET_PERSON_INFO.$output;\n\nlet combinedResults = [];\nlet profileDataMap = {};\nlet firstSeenIndex = {};\nlet seenContentTypes = {}; // Tracks unique content types per person\nlet globalAppearanceCounter = 0;\n\n// Step 1: Parse profile info, handle fail-safes, and track unique content types\nfor (let jsonString of searchCombinationResult) {\n    let parsed = typeof jsonString === 'string' ? JSON.parse(jsonString) : jsonString;\n    \n    // Fail-safe: Check if parsed object and results array exist\n    if (parsed && Array.isArray(parsed.results)) {\n        for (let item of parsed.results) {\n            // Fail-safe: Ensure item, metadata, and personId are present\n            if (!item || !item.metadata || item.metadata.personId === null || item.metadata.personId === undefined) {\n                continue; // Skip this malformed record safely\n            }\n\n            let pId = item.metadata.personId.toString();\n            let cType = item.metadata.contentType;\n\n            // Initialize tracking for a new personId\n            if (firstSeenIndex[pId] === undefined) {\n                firstSeenIndex[pId] = globalAppearanceCounter;\n                profileDataMap[pId] = [];\n                seenContentTypes[pId] = {};\n            }\n\n            // Enforce Unique Content Types (only keep the first/earliest one)\n            if (cType && !seenContentTypes[pId][cType]) {\n                seenContentTypes[pId][cType] = true; // Mark as seen\n                \n                profileDataMap[pId].push({\n                    contentType: cType,\n                    supportingChunks: item.supportingChunks || []\n                });\n            }\n            \n            globalAppearanceCounter++;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// Step 2: Merge personDetails items into a map\nlet personMap = {}; \n// Fail-safe: Ensure items array exists\nlet items = (personDetails && personDetails.items) ? personDetails.items : [];\n\nfor (let person of items) {\n    if (!person) continue;\n\n    let pIdRaw = person.PersonId || person.PersonNumber;\n    if (pIdRaw === null || pIdRaw === undefined) continue;\n    \n    let pId = pIdRaw.toString();\n\n    // Create entry for person if not already seen\n    if (!personMap[pId]) {\n        let highlights = profileDataMap[pId] || [];\n        personMap[pId] = {\n            personId: pId,\n            personNumber: person.PersonNumber,\n            displayName: person.DisplayName,\n            workEmail: person.WorkEmail,\n            assignments: [],\n            profileHighlights: highlights,\n            // Sorting attributes based on unique chunks only\n            _typeCount: highlights.length,\n            _firstAppearance: firstSeenIndex[pId] !== undefined ? firstSeenIndex[pId] : 999999\n        };\n    }\n\n    // Capture the assignment-specific fields safely\n    personMap[pId].assignments.push({\n        assignmentNumber: person.AssignmentNumber,\n        businessTitle: person.BusinessTitle,\n        jobName: person.JobName,\n        departmentName: person.DepartmentName,\n        locationName: person.LocationName,\n        positionName: person.PositionName,\n        gradeName: person.GradeName,\n        businessUnitName: person.BusinessUnitName,\n        legalEmployerName: person.LegalEmployerName,\n        city: person.City,\n        country: person.Country\n    });\n}\n\n// Step 3: Native Sort (O(n log n) instead of O(n^2))\nlet sortableArray = Object.values(personMap);\n\n// Using standard anonymous function for compatibility instead of an arrow function\nsortableArray.sort(function(a, b) {\n    // Rank by max number of unique contentTypes (descending)\n    if (b._typeCount !== a._typeCount) {\n        return b._typeCount - a._typeCount;\n    }\n    // Tie-breaker: Use the order they first appeared (ascending)\n    return a._firstAppearance - b._firstAppearance;\n});\n\n// Step 4: Extract Top 20 and push to final array\n// Using a simple loop to avoid chaining methods or expressions in the return\nlet limit = sortableArray.length < 20 ? sortableArray.length : 20;\n\nfor (let i = 0; i < limit; i++) {\n    let entry = sortableArray[i];\n    \n    combinedResults.push({\n        personId: entry.personId,\n        personNumber: entry.personNumber,\n        displayName: entry.displayName,\n        workEmail: entry.workEmail,\n        assignments: entry.assignments,\n        profileHighlights: entry.profileHighlights\n    });\n}\n\n// Single, simple return variable as required\nreturn combinedResults;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770904247029"
          },
          "code": "PREPARE_PERSON_DATA_FOR_RERANKING",
          "id": "1770904138856",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Answer question about person"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ANSWER_QUESTION_ABOUT_PERSON",
          "id": "1770902941177",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770902941178_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a deterministic, production-ready answer synthesis agent.\n\nYour job is to answer the user's question using the provided structured person data and render the response as clean, minimal HTML suitable for a mobile drawer (max-width: 600px).\n\n### INPUTS\n1. person_profile_data\n {{$context.$nodes.CLEAN_UP_PERSON_PROFILE_OUTPUT.$output.result}} \n\n2. user_query\n {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\n3. chat_history\n {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} \n\n4. base_person_profile_url\n {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_PERSON_PROFILE_DEEP_LINK.$output}}\n (A canonical URL ending in specific ID syntax, e.g., `.../101`)\n\n### STRICT FORMATTING PROTOCOL (CRITICAL)\n1. **Output Raw HTML Only**: Do NOT wrap the output in markdown code blocks (e.g., no ```html).\n2. **No Markdown Syntax**: Do NOT use `**` for bold or `_` for italics. \n   - CORRECT: `<b>Value</b>`, `<i>Value</i>`\n   - INCORRECT: `**Value**`, `*Value*`\n3. **Styling**: Use INLINE STYLES only. No `<style>` blocks.\n   - Font Family: `'Oracle Sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif`\n   - Text Color: `#101010`\n   - Label Color: `#6e6e6e`\n   - Borders: `1px solid #f0f0f0`\n\n### LOGIC: LINK CONSTRUCTION\nTo create a profile link for a specific person:\n1. Take `base_person_profile_url`.\n2. Locate the substring `101`.\n3. Replace `101` with the employee's `personId`.\n4. Use the result as the `href` in the anchor tag.\n\n---\n\n### STEP 1: DETERMINE RESPONSE MODE\n\n**MODE A: DIRECT ANSWER (Text Only)**\n- **Trigger**: Binary questions (\"Does John know Java?\"), single-fact lookups (\"What is her email?\"), or counts.\n- **Output**: A single `<p>` block.\n- **Style**: `<p style=\"font-family: 'Oracle Sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #101010; margin: 0;\">`\n- **Content**: Answer directly. Use `<b>` tags for the specific answer key.\n- **Example**: `<p style=\"...\"><b>Yes</b>, John lists Java as a competency.</p>`\n\n**MODE B: SUMMARY & COMPARISON (Table)**\n- **Trigger**: \"Show me X\", \"Compare X and Y\", \"List skills of X\", \"Find experts in X\".\n- **Output**: A Headline followed by a **Single Data Table**.\n\n---\n\n### STEP 2: MODE B EXECUTION (Table Construction)\n\n**1. Headline**\nGenerate: `<p style=\"font-family: 'Oracle Sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 20px;\">Here is the information you requested:</p>`\n\n**2. Spacer**\nGenerate: `<div style=\"height: 15px;\"></div>`\n\n**3. Data Table Logic**\nConstruct **ONE** table.\n- **Column Structure**:\n  - Column 1: Attribute Label (Fixed width: 25%)\n  - Columns 2 through N: One column per person found in `person_profile_data`. (Divide remaining 75% width equally).\n\n**4. Table Styling & Rows (CRITICAL FORMATTING)**\nUse the exact structure below. To prevent Markdown parsing errors, do NOT include any empty lines or indentation between the table tags. Apply border styles to the td tags, not the tr tags.\n\n<table style=\"width: 100%; max-width: 600px; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 25px; font-family: 'Oracle Sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%; color: #6e6e6e; font-size: 12px; padding: 8px 0; vertical-align: top; border-bottom: 1px solid #f0f0f0;\">Name</td><td style=\"color: #101010; font-size: 14px; padding: 8px 0; vertical-align: top; border-bottom: 1px solid #f0f0f0;\"><b><a href=\"{CONSTRUCTED_LINK}\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: #101010; text-decoration: underline;\">{DisplayName}</a></b></td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 25%; color: #6e6e6e; font-size: 12px; padding: 8px 0; vertical-align: top; border-bottom: 1px solid #f0f0f0;\">{Attribute Label}</td><td style=\"color: #101010; font-size: 14px; padding: 8px 0; vertical-align: top; border-bottom: 1px solid #f0f0f0;\">{Value}</td></tr>\n</table>\n\nINSUFFICIENT DATA RULE\n\nIf the required person cannot be identified or data is missing for the specific question:\n\nOutput: <p style=\"font-family: 'Oracle Sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #333333;\">I could not find the requested information in the available profiles.</p>\n\nFINAL INSTRUCTION\n\nAnalyze the User Query to select the mode. Generate the raw HTML string now. Ensure all column alignments are correct for side-by-side comparisons."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Craft final response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CRAFT_FINAL_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1770904247029",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770904247030_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Act as a Strategic Resource Manager. Use ONLY the provided context to answer the user's question.\n\n### Context (Combined Employee Profile Data):\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_PERSON_DATA_FOR_RERANKING.$output.result}}\n\n### User Question:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n### Query Plan:\n{{$context.$nodes.QUERY_PLANNER.$output}}\n\n### Person Profile URL:\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_PERSON_PROFILE_DEEP_LINK.$output}}\n\n### Location Mapping:\n{{$context.$nodes.RESOLVE_LOCATIONS.$output.results}}\n\n### Org Structure Mapping:\n{{$context.$nodes.RESOLVE_ORG_STRUCTURES.$output.results}}\n\n### SYSTEM INSTRUCTIONS\n\n<logic_protocol>\n1. INTENT ANALYSIS & DIMENSION MAPPING:\n   Analyze the User Question to determine which Data Dimensions are relevant:\n   - **\"Lead/Manage/Senior\":** Focus on Work History (Years of Experience, Management Titles) and Competency Levels.\n   - **\"Qualified/Certified/MBA\":** Focus on Certifications and Education.\n   - **\"French/Spanish Speaker\":** Focus on Language (prioritize 'Write'/'Teach' abilities over just 'Read').\n   - **\"Wants to do X/Future Leader\":** Focus on Career Preference and Career Statement.\n   - **\"Part-time/Contract\":** Focus on Work Preference.\n   - **\"Expert/Skilled\":** Focus on Skills (Proficiency Scores) and Competencies (Weights/Levels).\n\n2. FILTERING (Hard Constraints):\n   - Strict Location Match: If a city/country is specified, EXCLUDE all employees not in that location.\n   - Semantic Role/Skill Match: Eliminate candidates who lack the core required skill or its direct, highly specific equivalents (e.g., exact synonyms or specialized subsets of the requested skill). CRITICAL: Do NOT accept broad, generic categories or high-level disciplines as a substitute for a specific requested skill.\n\n3. DEEP RANKING (The \"Best Fit\" Algorithm):\n   Compare candidates based on the strength of evidence in the relevant dimensions:\n   * **Hierarchy of Evidence:**\n     1. **Current Capability:** (Job Title + Weighted Competencies + Skills).\n     2. **Proven History:** (Years of Experience in relevant Work History).\n     3. **Credentials:** (Specific Degrees or Certifications if requested).\n     4. **Aspirational Fit:** (Does their Career Preference/Statement align with the role? *Use this as a tie-breaker*).\n   * **Scoring Rules:**\n     - A \"Senior\" title with \"Weight: 4\" Competency OUTRANKS a \"Junior\" title with \"Weight: 4\".\n     - A candidate with \"Future Career Preference: Product Manager\" OUTRANKS others for a \"Product Owner\" role if skills are equal.\n\n4. SELECTION:\n   - Select the top N employees based on the Ranking Step.\n   - N = User specified quantity OR 3 if unspecified.\n</logic_protocol>\n\n<attribute_selection_logic>\nYou must dynamically construct the table rows based on the user's specific question and the available `profileHighlights`.\n\n**Mandatory Rows (Fixed Position):**\n   1. **Header:** Name\n   2. **Footer:** Match Justification\n\n**Dynamic Content Rows (Insert between Header and Footer):**\n   * **Contextual Identification (Separate Rows):** Evaluate the user's query to determine which identity attributes to display as distinct rows:\n       - **Job Title:** (Always show this to establish a baseline).\n       - **Location:** Generate this row ONLY if the query implies a geographic constraint or preference, or if location resolves a tie.\n       - **Department/Org:** Generate this row ONLY if the query involves specific teams, business units, or organizational structure.\n   * **Content Specifics (High Priority):** Check `profileHighlights` for the following types. IF present and relevant to the query, generate a distinct row for **EACH** type found:\n       - **Skill**: List specific matched skills.\n       - **Work History**: Summarize relevant roles/years.\n       - **Certification**: List credential names.\n       - **Education**: List degree/school.\n       - **Competency**: List competency and level.\n       - **Language**: List language and proficiency.\n       - **Career Preference**: Summary of preferences.\n       - **Career Statement**: Excerpt of the statement text (use bold for key terms).\n       - **Work Preference**: Summary of preferences.\n</attribute_selection_logic>\n\n<critical_constraints>\n1. **NO MARKDOWN SYMBOLS**:\n   - You are strictly FORBIDDEN from using `**`, `__`, or `##`.\n   - The rendering engine DOES NOT support Markdown. Usage will cause display bugs.\n   - You MUST use `<b>` for bold and `<i>` for italics.\n   - Do not mix Markdown and HTML. Ensure absolutely no asterisks (`*`) or hashes (`#`) are used for text formatting in the final output.\n   \n2. **LAYOUT RIGIDITY**:\n   - Do not rely on CSS margins for spacing between the headline and table.\n   - You MUST insert the \"Spacer Div\" defined in the templates below.\n\n3. **NO PREAMBLE (HEADLESS API MODE)**:\n   - You are a headless data-formatting API. Output ONLY the raw HTML. Do not acknowledge the prompt, do not say \"Here is the result\", and do not use formatting code blocks (like ```html).\n</critical_constraints>\n\n### OUTPUT GENERATION\n\n#### SCENARIO 1: NO MATCHES FOUND\nIf no employees match the criteria, output ONLY this exact HTML:\n<p style=\"font-family: 'Oracle Sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #333;\">No matching employees found.</p>\n\n#### SCENARIO 2: MATCHES FOUND\nIf matches are found, generate the output in this exact order:\n\n**1. Summary Headline**\nGenerate a single HTML paragraph. Select the template that matches the result count:\n* **If N=1:** `<p style=\"font-family: 'Oracle Sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #333;\">I found only the following employee matching your query for {criteria}:</p>`\n* **If N < 3 (Scarcity):** `<p style=\"font-family: 'Oracle Sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #333;\">I found only these {N} employees matching your query for {criteria}:</p>`\n* **If N >= 3 (Abundance):** `<p style=\"font-family: 'Oracle Sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #333;\">Here are the top {N} employees matching your query for {criteria}:</p>`\n\n**2. Spacer Block (Mandatory)**\n`<div style=\"height: 30px;\"></div>`\n\n**3. Employee Tables**\nFor each of the N selected employees, render this HTML block.\n*Note: The table content is dynamic. You MUST repeat the `<tr>` block for EVERY content type selected by the <attribute_selection_logic>.*\n\n<table style=\"width: 100%; max-width: 600px; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 25px; font-family: 'Oracle Sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">\n  \n  <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #f0f0f0;\">\n    <td style=\"width: 25%; color: #6e6e6e; font-size: 12px; padding: 5px 0; vertical-align: top;\">Name</td>\n    <td style=\"width: 75%; color: #101010; font-size: 14px; padding: 5px 0; vertical-align: top;\">\n      <b><a href=\"{PROFILE_LINK}\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: #101010; text-decoration: underline;\">{EMPLOYEE_NAME}</a></b>\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #f0f0f0;\">\n    <td style=\"width: 25%; color: #6e6e6e; font-size: 12px; padding: 5px 0; vertical-align: top;\">{Attribute_Name}</td>\n    <td style=\"width: 75%; color: #101010; font-size: 14px; padding: 5px 0; vertical-align: top;\">{Attribute_Value}</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #f0f0f0;\">\n    <td style=\"width: 25%; color: #6e6e6e; font-size: 12px; padding: 5px 0; vertical-align: top;\">Match Justification</td>\n    <td style=\"width: 75%; color: #101010; font-size: 14px; padding: 5px 0; vertical-align: top;\">\n      {JUSTIFICATION_TEXT}\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n**Link Logic:**\n- Construct `{PROFILE_LINK}` by replacing the final ID number at the end of the `Person Profile URL` with the employee's `{personId}`.\n\n**Emphasis & Content Rules (Strict HTML Only):**\n- **Bold:** Use `<b>` tags for exact skills/titles. (Example: `<b>Java</b>`, `<b>Manager</b>`).\n- **Italics:** Use `<i>` tags for context. (Example: `<i>5 years</i>`).\n- **Forbidden:** NEVER use `**` or `__`.\n- **Content:** The Justification MUST explain the ranking (e.g., \"Ranked #1 due to Senior title and Career Preference match\").\n\nFINAL CHECK: Ensure output contains ONLY the Headline <p>, the Spacer <div>, and the <table> elements. No preamble."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
