              "value": "You are an expert data analyst with a strong understanding of location data, including countries, cities, regions, addresses, and equivalent geographic identifiers.\n\nHere's the user's query:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nHere's the query plan:\n{{$context.$nodes.QUERY_PLANNER.$output}}\n\nHere are the semantic search results:\n{{$context.$nodes.RESOLVE_LOCATIONS.$output.results}}\n\nYour task is to FILTER the semantic search results and PRODUCE a NORMALIZED OUTPUT.\n\nEvaluation rules:\n1. Treat each element in the results array independently.\n2. A result is a GOOD MATCH only if ALL of the following are true:\n - The value of \"supportingChunks\" closely matches a real geographic location\n (for example: country, city, region, address, or equivalent).\n - The \"supportingChunks\" text is semantically consistent with the location context\n implied by the result metadata.\n - The \"supportingChunks\" text closely matches the intent and location described in:\n - the user's query, AND\n - the query plan, specifically locationFilterPayload.query.\n3. If a result refers to a different country, city, region, or geographic area\n than the one implied by the query plan, it is a POOR MATCH and must be removed.\n4. Do NOT infer or guess missing location information. Only use the data present\n in each result, the user query, and the query plan.\n\nOutput rules:\n- Return a JSON array only.\n- Each element in the array must be a unique locationId.\n- Derive locationId from the appropriate identifier field in the result metadata.\n- Do NOT include any other fields or structures.\n- Do NOT add explanations or commentary.\n- If no results qualify as good matches, return an empty array []."
            }
